{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#c8ac43fe-42db-413b-b240-c1fb6e9b45e8","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"c8ac43fe-42db-413b-b240-c1fb6e9b45e8","dateCreated":"2026-10-01T20:09:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-10-01T20:09:23+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/kinesis-video-streams-vpc-privatelink/","postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e now supports interface VPC endpoints powered by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/what-is-privatelink.html\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e, providing private connectivity from your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC). Traffic between your VPC and Kinesis Video Streams stays on the AWS network and is not exposed to the public internet, across the control plane and the video ingestion and playback data planes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCustomers with strict security, compliance, or network-isolation requirements can now ingest, store, and play back video without internet gateways, NAT devices, or public IP addresses. For example, connected-camera or IoT video workloads in a private subnet can send media to Kinesis Video Streams and retrieve it for playback and analytics entirely over private connectivity. You create the endpoint from the Amazon VPC console, AWS CLI, or AWS SDKs and can attach a VPC endpoint policy to control access.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVPC endpoints for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams are available in all AWS Regions where Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions and the China (Beijing) Region, operated by Beijing Sinnet Technology Co., Ltd. (\"Sinnet\").\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/vpc-interface-endpoints.html\"\u003eGetting Started Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","postDateTime":"2026-09-30T08:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams now supports VPC endpoints with AWS PrivateLink"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-privatelink","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-privatelink","description":"general:products/aws-privatelink","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-benefits-realized#security","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-benefits-realized","name":"security","description":"marketing:benefits-realized/security","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:28+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#amazon-kinesis-video-streams-kvs-now-supports-webrtc-in-aws-govcloud-us-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams-(kvs)-now-supports-webrtc-in-aws-govcloud-(us)-regions","dateCreated":"2026-04-06T22:05:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-04-06T22:24:59+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams (KVS) now supports WebRTC (Real-Time Communication) in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions, bringing real-time, low-latency media and data streaming to security-sensitive workloads in the cloud. Amazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely ingest, store, and process video from connected devices at scale. WebRTC support extends this capability to real-time, two-way media streaming, enabling sub-second latency for mission-critical applications.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this update, AWS customers and AWS Partners who operate in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions can now build and deploy real-time video streaming applications without compromising on compliance. For example, the update enables developers within these agencies to support critical use cases including live surveillance feeds for border security and military installations, real-time body camera streaming for law enforcement with data residency compliance, remote drone and UAV video monitoring for defense operations, and Internet of Things (IoT) smart infrastructure monitoring for state and local governments, all while meeting Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program (FedRAMP) High and other regulatory requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available today in AWS GovCloud (US-East) and AWS GovCloud (US-West). To get started, visit the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC product page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/availability.html\"\u003eAWS Region table\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/04/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-govcloud-regions/","postDateTime":"2026-03-30T22:30:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams (KVS) now supports WebRTC in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-hwp3jesktyudecrzqpbpeh","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-hwp3jesktyudecrzqpbpeh","dateCreated":"2025-12-17T01:17:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-23T21:35:22+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams (Amazon KVS) now supports Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6) addressing for WebRTC. This release introduces dual-stack endpoint support, enabling developers to use both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses to stream video from millions of devices. The dual-stack support is designed to ensure that existing IPv4 implementations continue to work reliably while gaining IPv6 connectivity benefits. Moreover, the update simplifies transition to IPv6 addresses while eliminating the need for address translation equipment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all commercial \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/availability.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon KVS is offered, except Asia Pacific (Singapore) and China (Beijing, operated by Sinnet). For implementation details, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/kvswebrtc-ipv6.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon KVS Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-ipv6/","postDateTime":"2025-12-22T18:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams now supports IPv6 for WebRTC"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-jdpbeeprgdlyq3ddwkhea3","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-jdpbeeprgdlyq3ddwkhea3","dateCreated":"2025-11-25T20:19:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-11-26T23:04:35+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS announces a new warm storage tier for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon KVS), delivering cost-effective storage for extended media retention. The standard Amazon KVS storage tier, now designated as the hot tier, remains optimized for real-time data access and short-term storage. The new warm tier enables long-term media retention with sub-second access latency at reduced storage costs.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThe warm storage tier enables developers of home security and enterprise video monitoring solutions to cost-effectively stream data from devices, cameras, and mobile phones while maintaining extended retention periods for video analytics and regulatory compliance. Moreover, developers now have the flexibility to configure fragment sizes based on their specific requirements — selecting smaller fragments for lower latency use cases or larger fragments to reduce ingestion costs. Both hot and warm storage tiers integrate seamlessly with Amazon Rekognition Video and Amazon SageMaker, enabling continuous data processing to support the creation of computer vision and video analytics applications.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAmazon Kinesis Video Streams with the new warm storage tier is available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available, except the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/tiered-storage.html\"\u003egetting started guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-warm-storage-tier/","postDateTime":"2025-11-26T18:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams now supports a new cost effective warm storage tier"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-qccu7fsguvdl3kg96o91ny","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-qccu7fsguvdl3kg96o91ny","dateCreated":"2025-10-13T21:02:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-11-13T21:55:57+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e now offers the ability to stream real-time audio and video to multiple concurrent viewers via WebRTC, while also recording video and audio from the session to the cloud for storage, playback, and analytical processing. With this update, developers can enable up to 3 concurrent viewers of real-time feeds from cameras or other video-producing devices without increasing compute or bandwidth utilization on the device. In addition, participants can engage in audio conversations with each other, enabling direct real-time communication between viewers during the session.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nDevelopers can now build real-time peer-to-peer streaming applications by installing the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-c/tree/wrtc-stream-ingestion-support\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC SDK\u003c/a\u003e across security cameras, IoT devices, PCs, and mobile devices. Using the APIs, developers can create applications that stream real-time media to multiple concurrent viewers. They can develop solutions for scenarios such as home security applications sharing camera feeds with family members, remote proctoring systems with multiple monitoring operators, or robot operation control centers with audit capabilities. Developers can implement both live and on-demand video playback through session recording, and build advanced applications utilizing computer vision and video analytics by integrating with Amazon Rekognition Video and Amazon SageMaker.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAmazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC Multi-Viewer is available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available, except the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions and the China (Beijing, operated by Sinnet) Region.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/webrtc-ingestion.html\"\u003eGetting Started Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-multi-viewer/","postDateTime":"2025-11-13T08:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC Multi-Viewer"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#media-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"media-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/media-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-th8kaeryanjvbwfxjv2dfe","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-th8kaeryanjvbwfxjv2dfe","dateCreated":"2025-08-28T17:20:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-10-17T17:07:21+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6) addressing support for\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003e Amazon Kinesis Video Streams (KVS)\u003c/a\u003e. With this enhancement, KVS now offers dual-stack endpoints that let customers use both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses to stream video from millions of devices. This means that existing IPv4 implementations continue to work seamlessly while gaining the benefits of IPv6 connectivity.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAs customers increasingly encounter IPv4 address exhaustion in their private networks, this enhancement delivers much-needed flexibility. Organizations can now seamlessly stream videos using IPv4, IPv6, or dual-stack clients. This advancement simplifies IPv6-based system transitions, ensures compliance requirements are met, and eliminates dependency on costly address translation equipment.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nIPv6 support is available in all commercial\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/availability.html\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;where Amazon KVS is available except Ap-Southeast-1 and AWS GovCloud (US-West) regions\u0026nbsp;. To learn more about Amazon KVS, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/what-is-kinesis-video.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/10/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-ipv6-streams-capability/","postDateTime":"2025-10-03T16:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams now supports IPv6 for Streams capability"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p105993082","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"nYyvJFzqSnKzwJfEjF8ioX","dateCreated":"2024-05-16T18:39:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-06-18T18:03:53+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams is now available in AWS GovCloud (US-East and US-West) Regions. Amazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for storage, analytics, machine learning (ML), playback, and other processing. Amazon Kinesis Video Streams automatically provisions and elastically scales all the infrastructure needed to ingest streaming video data from millions of devices. It durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access your data through easy-to-use APIs. Kinesis Video Streams enables you to playback video for live and on-demand viewing, and quickly build applications that take advantage of computer vision and video analytics through integration with Amazon Rekognition Video and Amazon Sagemaker.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page,\u003c/a\u003e and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information. Note that Amazon Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC is not yet available in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/06/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-aws-govcloud-regions/","postDateTime":"2024-06-18T10:00:00-07:00","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is now available in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-image-sampling-frequency","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-image-sampling-frequency/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:01:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:50:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces improvements to the image extraction functionality within Amazon Kinesis Video Streams. Now customers can extract images at a rate of 5 frames per second, improved from one image every 3 seconds. Customers can now use high frequency sampling for ML inferencing and a rich playback experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams image extraction is a fully-managed capability that allows customers to request images via API calls or configure automatic image generation from ingested video. Images can be leveraged in machine learning pipelines, including Amazon Sagemaker, Amazon Rekognition, or custom solutions. Customers can also use this capability for enhanced playback applications such as thumbnails or enhanced timeline scrubbing.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eImage extraction capabilities are available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available. To learn more, see documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/images.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-15T19:14:47Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-image-sampling-frequency/","postDateTime":"2023-08-15T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams improves image sampling frequency to 5 frames per second","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces improvements to the image extraction functionality within Amazon Kinesis Video Streams. Now customers can extract images at a rate of 5 frames per second, improved from one image every 3 seconds. Customers can now use high frequency sampling for ML inferencing and a rich playback experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-ingestion-storage-webrtc-preview","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-ingestion-storage-webrtc-preview/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:51:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:36:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams now offers fully managed capabilities to stream video and audio in real-time from Web Real-Time Communication (WebRTC) standards compliant cameras, IoT devices and browsers to the cloud for secured storage, playback and analytical processing. Customers can now use our enhanced WebRTC SDK and cloud APIs to enable real-time streaming as well as media ingestion to the cloud.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you can install the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-c/tree/wrtc-stream-ingestion-support\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC SDK\u003c/a\u003e on any security camera or IoT device with a video sensor, and use our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_Operations_Amazon_Kinesis_Video_Streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAPIs\u003c/a\u003e to enable media streaming with sub 1-second latency, as well as ingestion and storage in the cloud. Once ingested, you can access your data through our easy-to-use APIs. Amazon Kinesis Video Streams enables you to playback video for live and on-demand viewing, and quickly build applications that take advantage of computer vision and video analytics through integration with Amazon Rekognition Video and Amazon SageMaker.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams ingestion via WebRTC is available in preview in the US West (Oregon) region. To learn more about these new capabilities for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/webrtc-ingestion.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGetting Started Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-02-08T19:35:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-ingestion-storage-webrtc-preview/","postDateTime":"2022-12-21T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams announces ingestion and storage support for Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC (Preview)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams now offers fully managed capabilities to stream video and audio in real-time from Web Real-Time Communication (WebRTC) standards compliant cameras, IoT devices and browsers to the cloud for secured storage, playback and analytical processing. Customers can now use our enhanced WebRTC SDK and cloud APIs to enable real-time streaming as well as media ingestion to the cloud.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#media-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"media-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/media-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-05-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-managed-support-image-extraction","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-managed-support-image-extraction/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:51:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:19:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday Amazon Kinesis Video Streams announces new APIs and SDKs to help you extract images from your video streams. This fully-managed capability allows customers to request images via API calls or configure automatic image generation based on metadata tags in ingested video.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can use this new functionality to generate images for playback applications such as thumbnails or enhanced timeline scrubbing. They can also generate images for Machine Learning pipelines, including Amazon Sagemaker, Amazon Rekognition, or custom solutions.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThese features are available in all regions where Kinesis Video Streams is available. Image extraction will cost $10 per million images for streams of resolution up to and including 1080p, or $18 per million images for streams or resolution greater than 1080p up to 4K.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;To get started with this feature, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/images.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-05T13:50:39Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-managed-support-image-extraction/","postDateTime":"2022-05-04T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams announces managed support for image extraction","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday Amazon Kinesis Video Streams announces new APIs and SDKs to help you extract images from your video streams. This fully-managed capability allows customers to request images via API calls or configure automatic image generation based on metadata tags in ingested video.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-updates-media-playback-api-service-quotas-to-enable-up-to-10x-more-simultaneous-consumers","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-updates-media-playback-api-service-quotas-to-enable-up-to-10x-more-simultaneous-consumers/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:01:58+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams (KVS)\u003c/a\u003e updates the service quota model for its media playback APIs to throttle based on the number of fragments requested rather than the number of playback sessions. This gives developers the flexibility to enable up to 10x more simultaneous playback sessions for applications that use Kinesis Video Streams for live or on-demand playback.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers can use simple playback APIs to enable HTTP Live Streaming (HLS) or Dynamic Adaptive Streaming over HTTP (DASH) based live or on-demand playback for media streamed to a Kinesis video stream. Previously, these APIs were throttled by the rate at which they were called and applications were limited to a maximum of 10 live or on-demand simultaneous playback sessions. This limit for maximum playback sessions is now removed and replaced with the new quota model, in which the HLS and DASH APIs are rate-limited across all sessions by the number of fragment metadata and the number of media fragments requested. This gives developers the flexibility to create 100 or more simultaneous playback sessions by programmatically selecting the size of metadata and number of media fragments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to more simultaneous sessions, KVS API for session creation rate limits are updated to 25 requests per second.  This allows developers to create more playback sessions quickly (e.g., an application can now create 10 playback sessions in 1 second whereas previously creating 10 sessions would take 6 seconds). Finally, this change also enables developers to request up to 5x longer playlists for on-demand playback and avoid frequent playlist refreshes. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about this new service quota model, please refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/limits.html#fragment_based_throttling\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.  \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-03-10T21:58:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-updates-media-playback-api-service-quotas-to-enable-up-to-10x-more-simultaneous-consumers/","postDateTime":"2021-03-10T18:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams updates media playback API service quotas to enable up to 10x more simultaneous consumers","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams (KVS)\u003c/a\u003e updates the service quota model for its media playback APIs to throttle based on the number of fragments requested rather than the number of playback sessions. This gives developers the flexibility to enable up to 10x more simultaneous playback sessions for applications that use Kinesis Video Streams for live or on-demand playback.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-in-c-supports-client-metrics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-in-c-supports-client-metrics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:15:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e adds client metrics support to its WebRTC SDK in C. Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC enables developers to build web, mobile, and IoT devices application for real-time media and data streaming. Developers can use this capability to build applications for use cases such as home security and monitoring, camera-enabled doorbells, baby and pet monitoring, smart appliances, and more. Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK in C enables IoT devices to securely connect with Kinesis Video Streams for peer discovery and media streaming. The client metrics allows developers to monitor and track performance of the applications built using the WebRTC SDK in C. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC client metrics include metrics for WebRTC signaling and multiple \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.w3.org/TR/webrtc-stats/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eW3C standards\u003c/a\u003e compliant metrics for networking, media, and data streaming. Developers can use simple APIs to obtain various metrics to monitor application behaviors such as connectivity states, connection latencies, and statistics for media or data streaming. For example, developers can monitor media streaming quality by tracking the data packet loss as percentage of data packets exchanged for an outbound stream in a specific duration. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams support for WebRTC, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/what-is-kvswebrtc.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about the client metrics included in Amazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK in C and for examples, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/kvswebrtc-reference.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-13T20:07:45Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-in-c-supports-client-metrics/","postDateTime":"2020-11-13T12:27:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK in C now supports client metrics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e adds client metrics support to its WebRTC SDK in C. Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC enables developers to build web, mobile, and IoT devices application for real-time media and data streaming. Developers can use this capability to build applications for use cases such as home security and monitoring, camera-enabled doorbells, baby and pet monitoring, smart appliances, and more. Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK in C enables IoT devices to securely connect with Kinesis Video Streams for peer discovery and media streaming. The client metrics allows developers to monitor and track performance of the applications built using the WebRTC SDK in C. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#media-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"media-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/media-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-api-support-to-easily-retrieve-media-clips","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-api-support-to-easily-retrieve-media-clips/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:10:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e adds a new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_reader_GetClip.html\"\u003eGetClip API\u003c/a\u003e that makes it easy for developers to retrieve media stored in their Kinesis video streams. Developers can use the API to synchronously generate MP4 clips for offline playback, sharing playable clips, long term archival of interesting events, file based processing via Machine Learning applications, and other use cases.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers can use the GetClip API by providing the video stream name or its Amazon Resource Name (ARN) where the data is stored, and a time range of media to be included in the clip. The API will then synchronously package the selected media in MP4 format and return it through the API. The API supports video data in H.264 or H.265 encoding formats, and audio data in AAC or G.711 encoding formats. The GetClip API is available via the AWS SDKs for all supported languages.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, you pay only for what you use. See Amazon Kinesis Video Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/pricing/\"\u003epricing\u003c/a\u003e for details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams and the GetClip API, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/what-is-kinesis-video.html\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-29T20:00:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-api-support-to-easily-retrieve-media-clips/","postDateTime":"2020-04-29T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams adds API support to easily retrieve media clips ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e adds a new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_reader_GetClip.html\"\u003eGetClip API\u003c/a\u003e that makes it easy for developers to retrieve media stored in their Kinesis video streams. Developers can use the API to synchronously generate MP4 clips for offline playback, sharing playable clips, long term archival of interesting events, file based processing via Machine Learning applications, and other use cases.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-available-nine-more-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-available-nine-more-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:22:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:24:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e is now available in nine additional AWS regions: US East (Ohio), Canada (Central), South America (São Paulo), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), and Asia Pacific (Singapore).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, playback, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. Kinesis Video Streams automatically provisions and elastically scales all the infrastructure needed to ingest streaming video data in real time from millions of devices. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access and playback your data through easy-to-use APIs. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams also supports real-time media streaming via WebRTC that enables developers to easily stream real-time two-way media for use cases like home security and monitoring, camera-enabled doorbells, baby and pet monitoring, camera-enabled vacuums, smart home automation, smart appliances, and more.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on AWS regions and services, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, please see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/what-is-kinesis-video.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-19T19:01:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-available-nine-more-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-12-19T10:45:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is now available in nine more regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e is now available in nine additional AWS regions: US East (Ohio), Canada (Central), South America (São Paulo), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), and Asia Pacific (Singapore).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#media-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"media-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/media-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-07-kinesis-video-streams-adds-support-for-dynamic-adaptive-streaming-over-http-dash-and-h-2-6-5-video","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/kinesis-video-streams-adds-support-for-dynamic-adaptive-streaming-over-http-dash-and-h-2-6-5-video/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:17:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Dynamic Adaptive Streaming over HTTP (DASH) capability enables developers to playback their ingested video streams using the industry-standard, HTTP-based media streaming protocol.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs devices stream their video into Kinesis Video Streams, developers can use the fully-managed DASH capability to playback live and recorded video from their streams. Developers can now also stream, store, and process H.265 video for playback and Machine Leaning based processing.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  The DASH-based playback capability is fully managed, so you do not have to build any cloud-based infrastructure or software to playback the media captured by Amazon Kinesis Video streams. You can simply create a streaming session using the new APIs and leverage webplayers such as VideoJS or GoogleShaka player, modern web browsers, or video players for mobile platforms such as Android (Exoplayer) and iOS (AVMediaPlayer), that are compatible with the fragmented MP4 (FMP4) format.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eH.265 video offers superior compression over H.264 encoded video allowing developers to deliver high quality video at lower bitrates. Developers can stream and store H.265 video generated by compatible edge devices into Kinesis Video streams and then process it for generating machine learning based insights or playback the video using Amazon Kinesis Video Streams’ HTTP Live Streaming (HLS) or DASH capabilities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/what-is-kinesis-video.html\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:37Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/kinesis-video-streams-adds-support-for-dynamic-adaptive-streaming-over-http-dash-and-h-2-6-5-video/","postDateTime":"2019-07-12T15:19:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Kinesis Video Streams adds support for Dynamic Adaptive Streaming over HTTP (DASH) and H.265 video","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Dynamic Adaptive Streaming over HTTP (DASH) capability enables developers to playback their ingested video streams using the industry-standard, HTTP-based media streaming protocol.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-07-announcing-availability-of-amazon-kinesis-video-producer-sdk-in-c","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/announcing-availability-of-amazon-kinesis-video-producer-sdk-in-c/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:18:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:22:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e producer SDKs are free and open software libraries for building applications that can stream audio and video data directly from an edge device to the AWS cloud for durable storage, playback, and machine learning based processing. Amazon Kinesis Video Streams producer SDK is now available in C.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the addition of producer SDK in C, developers can now choose among C, C++, and JAVA SDKs to build streaming applications that best suits their edge device platform. Producer SDK in C is specifically useful for building applications for edge devices with limited flash storage such as cameras used in home or enterprise security. An application built with the producer SDK in C can be deployed to an edge device with as low as 500KB of available flash storage.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Producer SDK in C is available for Linux, MacOS, Windows, and Raspbian platforms; and is also available as a Docker container for easy deployment. To learn more, please refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk.html\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:37Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/announcing-availability-of-amazon-kinesis-video-producer-sdk-in-c/","postDateTime":"2019-07-12T13:56:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing the availability of Amazon Kinesis Video Producer SDK in C","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e producer SDKs are free and open software libraries for building applications that can stream audio and video data directly from an edge device to the AWS cloud for durable storage, playback, and machine learning based processing. Amazon Kinesis Video Streams producer SDK is now available in C.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-03-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-is-now-available-in-asia-pacific-sydney","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-is-now-available-in-asia-pacific-sydney/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:17:57+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Asia Pacific (Sydney) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, playback, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. Kinesis Video Streams automatically provisions and elastically scales all the infrastructure needed to ingest streaming video data in real-time from millions of devices. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access and playback your data through easy-to-use APIs. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can use Amazon Kinesis Video Streams in the following AWS regions: US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), Europe (Ireland), Europe (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and Asia Pacific (Sydney). For more information on AWS regions and services, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, please see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/what-is-kinesis-video.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-is-now-available-in-asia-pacific-sydney/","postDateTime":"2019-03-07T10:31:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is Now Available in Asia Pacific (Sydney)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Asia Pacific (Sydney) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-02-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-synchronized-audio-video-playback-and-mpeg-ts-container-format-support-via-http-live-streaming-hls","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-synchronized-audio-video-playback-and-mpeg-ts-container-format-support-via-http-live-streaming-hls/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:09:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-03-12T22:10:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e enables developers to use its fully-managed HLS capability for synchronized audio video (AV) playback and also output HLS streams in MPEG-TS container format. Developers can now ingest both audio and video in a single multi-track Kinesis Video stream and use HLS APIs to deliver pre-segmented files and playlists in fragmented MP4 (fMP4) and MPEG-TS container formats for playback on compatible mobile and web players.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs an increasing number of camera-enabled devices now include a microphone, developers want to ingest both audio and video data in a Kinesis Video stream and build player applications for synchronized AV playback. Developers can now enable this capability by ingesting both video (H.264) and audio (AAC) in a single multi-track Kinesis Video stream. As the media is ingested, developers can then use KVS HLS APIs to playback the ingested media in both live and on-demand mode. Kinesis Video Streams now also allows developers to deliver media in both fMP4 and MPEG-TS as the HLS output container, increasing compatibility with earlier generation platforms such as iOS9.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producersdk-cpp-write.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproducer integration guide\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about ingesting audio and video data in a single Kinesis Video stream. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:47Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-synchronized-audio-video-playback-and-mpeg-ts-container-format-support-via-http-live-streaming-hls/","postDateTime":"2019-02-22T16:48:15Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams adds Synchronized Audio Video Playback and MPEG-TS Container Format Support via HTTP Live Streaming (HLS)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e enables developers to use its fully-managed HLS capability for synchronized audio video (AV) playback and also output HLS streams in MPEG-TS container format. Developers can now ingest both audio and video in a single multi-track Kinesis Video stream and use HLS APIs to deliver pre-segmented files and playlists in fragmented MP4 (fMP4) and MPEG-TS container formats for playback on compatible mobile and web players.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:08:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  AWS will use commercially reasonable efforts to make Amazon Kinesis Video Streams available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage, during any monthly billing cycle, of at least 99.9% (the “Service Commitment”). In the event Amazon Kinesis Video Streams does not meet the Service Commitment, you will be eligible to receive a Service Credit as described in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/sla/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams Service Level Agreement\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  This SLA is now available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available. For more information on availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","postDateTime":"2019-01-14T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Announces 99.9% Service Level Agreement","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-analyze-live-video-at-scale-in-real-time-using-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-and-amazon-sagemaker","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/analyze-live-video-at-scale-in-real-time-using-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-and-amazon-sagemaker/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-03-12T22:08:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now analyze live video at scale in real time using the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Inference Template (KIT) for Amazon SageMaker. The KIT enables you to build scalable, real-time, ML-driven video analytics pipelines without using other libraries or writing custom software. You can attach Kinesis video streams to Amazon SageMaker endpoints in minutes and quickly deploy your machine learning algorithms to analyze live video feeds on the AWS Cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe KIT contains the Kinesis Video Consumer Library software packaged as a Docker container and an AWS CloudFormation template that automates the deployment of all required AWS resources. The KIT also comes with a step-by-step example of integrating Amazon Kinesis Video Streams to Amazon SageMaker.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e makes it easy to securely stream audio, video, and related metadata from connected devices to AWS for analytics, machine learning (ML), playback, and other processing. \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/sagemaker.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SageMaker\u003c/a\u003e is the managed platform for developers and data scientists to build, train, and deploy ML models quickly and easily.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Inference Template, refer to our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/examples-sagemaker.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/analyze-live-video-at-scale-in-real-time-using-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-and-amazon-sagemaker/","postDateTime":"2018-11-20T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Analyze live video at scale in real-time using Amazon Kinesis Video Streams and Amazon SageMaker","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now analyze live video at scale in real time using the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Inference Template (KIT) for Amazon SageMaker. The KIT enables you to build scalable, real-time, ML-driven video analytics pipelines without using other libraries or writing custom software. You can attach Kinesis video streams to Amazon SageMaker endpoints in minutes and quickly deploy your machine learning algorithms to analyze live video feeds on the AWS Cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-kinesis-video-streams-fragment-level-metadata-support","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/kinesis-video-streams-fragment-level-metadata-support/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e now enables you to easily add metadata to and retrieve from individual fragments in a Kinesis Video stream to build richer applications in the AWS cloud. For example, you can now send GPS values as metadata with each video fragment from an on-person camera, or send temperature values with videos fragments from a baby monitor, and then use both the metadata and video fragments in your consuming applications to create richer user experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA fragment represents a segment of video, audio, or other time-encoded data. Metadata in Kinesis Video Streams is a mutable key-value pair that can be used to describe the content of the fragment, embed associated sensor readings, or any other custom data that needs to be transferred along with the actual fragment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFragment-level metadata gives you granular control over passing and processing additional information with each video fragment. The metadata is stored along with the video fragment for the entire duration of the stream\u0027s retention period. You can use it to embed GPS or temperature sensor values to video fragments that your consuming application can then use for creating meaningful correlations, or you can use it to mark exactly those video fragments that contain motion detected by your edge device, like a camera. Your deep-learning cloud application can then use this metadata to inform the next stage of processing such as identifying faces or objects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour stream producing application or device can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKinesis Video Producer SDK\u003c/a\u003e to add metadata to a video fragment. Your consuming application can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/parser-library.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKinesis Video Stream Parser Library\u003c/a\u003e to easily retrieve the metadata for each fragment via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_dataplane_GetMedia.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetMedia\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_reader_GetMediaForFragmentList.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetMediaForFragmentList\u003c/a\u003e API operations for further processing. To learn more, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/how-meta.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/kinesis-video-streams-fragment-level-metadata-support/","postDateTime":"2018-10-04T13:26:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams now supports adding and retrieving Metadata at Fragment-Level","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e now enables you to easily add metadata to and retrieve from individual fragments in a Kinesis Video stream to build richer applications in the AWS cloud. For example, you can now send GPS values as metadata with each video fragment from an on-person camera, or send temperature values with videos fragments from a baby monitor, and then use both the metadata and video fragments in your consuming applications to create richer user experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA fragment represents a segment of video, audio, or other time-encoded data. Metadata in Kinesis Video Streams is a mutable key-value pair that can be used to describe the content of the fragment, embed associated sensor readings, or any other custom data that needs to be transferred along with the actual fragment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFragment-level metadata gives you granular control over passing and processing additional information with each video fragment. The metadata is stored along with the video fragment for the entire duration of the stream\u0027s retention period. You can use it to embed GPS or temperature sensor values to video fragments that your consuming application can then use for creating meaningful correlations, or you can use it to mark exactly those video fragments that contain motion detected by your edge device, like a camera. Your deep-learning cloud application can then use this metadata to inform the next stage of processing such as identifying faces or objects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour stream producing application or device can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKinesis Video Producer SDK\u003c/a\u003e to add metadata to a video fragment. Your consuming application can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/parser-library.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKinesis Video Stream Parser Library\u003c/a\u003e to easily retrieve the metadata for each fragment via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_dataplane_GetMedia.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetMedia\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_reader_GetMediaForFragmentList.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetMediaForFragmentList\u003c/a\u003e API operations for further processing. To learn more, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/how-meta.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-08-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-windows","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-windows/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:55:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Producer SDK is now available for Microsoft Windows to help you stream video into AWS from sources such as webcams, USB cameras, or RTSP (network) cameras connected to your Microsoft Windows machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from millions of connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access your data through easy-to-use APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Video Streams provides Producer SDKs in C++ and Java that you can build, configure, and install on devices. This software makes it easier to securely and reliably stream video into AWS frame-by-frame in real-time. In addition to Mac OS, Android, Linux, and Raspbian, the C++ Producer SDK is now also available for Microsoft Windows. Developers can use the Minimal GNU for Windows (MinGW) or the Microsoft Visual Studio C++ Compiler (MSVC) to build the producer SDK from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-cpp\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esource\u003c/a\u003e and start streaming from cameras connected to a Microsoft Windows machine. Additionally, we have also packaged the Producer SDK GStreamer Plug-in for Windows as a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/examples-gstreamer-plugin.html#examples-gstreamer-plugin-docker-download\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDocker image\u003c/a\u003e so you can simply do a Docker pull and get started with streaming video in minutes. Please refer the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk-win.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e to learn more. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-windows/","postDateTime":"2018-08-31T19:02:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Producer SDK Is Now Available For Microsoft Windows","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Producer SDK is now available for Microsoft Windows to help you stream video into AWS from sources such as webcams, USB cameras, or RTSP (network) cameras connected to your Microsoft Windows machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from millions of connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access your data through easy-to-use APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Video Streams provides Producer SDKs in C++ and Java that you can build, configure, and install on devices. This software makes it easier to securely and reliably stream video into AWS frame-by-frame in real-time. In addition to Mac OS, Android, Linux, and Raspbian, the C++ Producer SDK is now also available for Microsoft Windows. Developers can use the Minimal GNU for Windows (MinGW) or the Microsoft Visual Studio C++ Compiler (MSVC) to build the producer SDK from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-cpp\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esource\u003c/a\u003e and start streaming from cameras connected to a Microsoft Windows machine. Additionally, we have also packaged the Producer SDK GStreamer Plug-in for Windows as a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/examples-gstreamer-plugin.html#examples-gstreamer-plugin-docker-download\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDocker image\u003c/a\u003e so you can simply do a Docker pull and get started with streaming video in minutes. Please refer the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk-win.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e to learn more. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-kinesis-video-adds-hls-support","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/kinesis-video-adds-hls-support/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:03:34+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Kinesis Video Streams’ HTTP Live Streaming (HLS) capability enables developers to playback their ingested video streams using the industry-standard, HTTP-based media streaming protocol. As devices stream their video into Kinesis Video Streams, developers can use the fully-managed HLS capability to playback live and recorded video from their streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. Kinesis Video Streams automatically provisions and elastically scales all the infrastructure needed to ingest streaming video data in real-time from millions of devices. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access and playback your data and video streams through easy-to-use APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe HLS-based playback capability is fully managed, so you do not have to build any cloud-based infrastructure or software to view the H.264 media captured by Amazon Kinesis Video streams. You can simply create a streaming session using the new API and leverage webplayers such as VideoJS or GoogleShaka player, modern web browsers, or video players for mobile platforms such as Android (Exoplayer) and iOS (AVMediaPlayer), that are compatible with the fragmented MP4 (FMP4) format.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can get started with the HLS-capability by following the example in this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-support-for-hls-output-streams\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/how-hls.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/kinesis-video-adds-hls-support/","postDateTime":"2018-07-13T21:55:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Kinesis Video Streams now supports HTTP Live Streaming (HLS) to playback live and recorded video from devices","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Kinesis Video Streams’ HTTP Live Streaming (HLS) capability enables developers to playback their ingested video streams using the industry-standard, HTTP-based media streaming protocol. As devices stream their video into Kinesis Video Streams, developers can use the fully-managed HLS capability to playback live and recorded video from their streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-06-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-gstreamer-plugin-and-docker-images","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/Kinesis_Video_Streams_Producer_SDK_Gstreamer_Plugin_and_Docker_Images/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:26:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Producer SDK is now available as a Gstreamer-plugin, and as Docker-images for Ubuntu, MacOS, and Raspberry Pi devices to help you stream video into AWS in minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. Kinesis Video Streams automatically provisions and elastically scales all the infrastructure needed to ingest streaming video data in real-time from millions of devices. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access your data through easy-to-use APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams provides Producer SDKs in C++ and Java that you can build, configure, and install on devices. This software makes it easier to securely and reliably stream video into AWS frame-by-frame in real-time. The Kinesis Video Producer SDK in C++ is now also available as a GStreamer-plugin. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGStreamer\u003c/a\u003e is a widely used, open source framework that provides a standard managed environment for constructing media-data flows from the device (camera or other video source) for further processing, rendering, or storage. Developers can use the Kinesis Video Producer GStreamer plugin to simplify their device-side application integration as they can take advantage of existing codecs and filter technology already available within GStreamer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers can build the individual Kinesis Video Producer and GStreamer components from sources available \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-cpp\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e, and fully customize their media pipeline for streaming into Kinesis Video. Additionally, we have also packaged the components as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk-cpp-gstreamer-docker.html\"\u003eDocker images\u003c/a\u003e for Ubuntu, MacOS, and Raspberry Pi devices. You can simply do a Docker pull and get started with streaming video in minutes.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/Kinesis_Video_Streams_Producer_SDK_Gstreamer_Plugin_and_Docker_Images/","postDateTime":"2018-06-20T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Kinesis Video Streams Producer SDK Gstreamer Plugin and Docker Images","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Producer SDK is now available as a Gstreamer-plugin, and as Docker-images for Ubuntu, MacOS, and Raspberry Pi devices to help you stream video into AWS in minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-11-introducing-amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/11/introducing-amazon-kinesis-video-streams/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:54:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                 Customers use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis\u003c/a\u003e to run real-time analytics using data streams. Today, we are adding video streams to Kinesis. We are announcing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e, a fully managed video ingestion and storage service. Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for machine learning, analytics, and processing. You can also stream other time-encoded data like RADAR and LIDAR signals using Kinesis Video Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Video Streams provides you SDKs you can install on your devices to make it easy and secure to stream video to AWS. It automatically provisions and elastically scales all the infrastructure needed to ingest video streams from millions of devices. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes the video streams and provides easy-to-use APIs so that applications can access and retrieve indexed video fragments based on tags and timestamps. Kinesis Video Streams provides a library to integrate ML frameworks such as Apache MxNet, Tensorflow, and OpenCV with video streams to build machine learning applications. Kinesis Video Streams is integrated with Amazon Rekognition Video, enabling you to build computer vision applications that detect objects, events, and people in videos. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eKinesis Video Streams website\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, create and configure a Kinesis video stream with a few clicks from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. You can then install the Kinesis Video Streams SDK on your devices and start streaming data to AWS for analytics, processing, and storage. With Kinesis Video Streams, you pay only for what you use. There are no upfront commitments or minimum fees. To learn more, see the Kinesis Video Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/what-is-kinesis-video.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                 Kinesis Video Streams is available in the US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:54:54Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/11/introducing-amazon-kinesis-video-streams/","postDateTime":"2017-11-29T14:48:05Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon Kinesis Video Streams","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                 Customers use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis\u003c/a\u003e to run real-time analytics using data streams. Today, we are adding video streams to Kinesis. We are announcing \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e, a fully managed video ingestion and storage service. Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for machine learning, analytics, and processing. You can also stream other time-encoded data like RADAR and LIDAR signals using Kinesis Video Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":25,"totalHits":25},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}